  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="f-6" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;6. See Entergy Louisiana's 2026 FERC Form 3Q For the Quarterly Period Ended June 30, 2026 Notes to Financial Statements, Note 4.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="f-7" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;7. None&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="f-8" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;8. Effective April 1, 2026, executive and senior management, middle management, professionals, and non-represented operating, maintenance, and support staff pay increases averaged approximately 3.49%.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;River Bend&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Security employees are represented by the International Union, Security, Police and Fire Professionals of America, Local Union 707. The Company and the Union agreed to a contract effective May 1, 2021 through April 30, 2024. The Company and the Union agreed to a contract extension effective through April 30, 2027 and have subsequently agreed to a new contract effective May 1, 2027 through April 30, 2031. Effective May 1, 2026, the wage increase was 2.0%.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Planners are represented by the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers, AFL-CIO, Local Union 2286. The Company and the Union agreed to a contract effective July 19, 2025 through July 18, 2029. Effective April 1, 2026, the wage increase was approximately 3.49%.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="f-9" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9. See Entergy Louisiana&#8217;s 2025 FERC Form 1 Notes to Financial Statements, Notes 2 and 8. See Entergy Louisiana&#8217;s 2026 FERC Form 3Q For the Quarterly Period Ended June 30, 2026 Notes to Financial Statements, Notes 1 and 2.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
